 "C0": {
  "code": "INELIG",
  "loc": "Abstract, p.1; Sect. 2, p.4",
  "quote": "A novel axiomatization of relative utilitarianism is provided using the single-profile",
  "note": "The paper axiomatizes a social welfare criterion (relative utilitarianism). A social observer's preference aggregates individual expected-utility preferences in a single-profile Harsanyi setting. No voting procedure, ballots or submitted inputs are involved. This is welfare-economic aggregation, not aggregation by voting. Borderline case: the paper is social choice theory, but it falls outside the voting scope as written. Coding stopped."
